ar teamwork data.\n**Main trade\u2011off:** Whether B\u2019s technical and stress strengths outweigh the unknowns about his decision speed and crew interaction, versus C\u2019s proven decision speed and reliability offset by his communication challenges.\n**Remaining uncertainty:**\n- B\u2019s decision\u2011making speed and how his interpersonal style translates into real crew dynamics.\n- C\u2019s actual effectiveness in crew communication despite difficulty expressing ideas, and whether his egocentric attitude leads to conflict.\n- Any concrete evidence of A\u2019s or D\u2019s teamwork/leadership performance.\n**What would change my vote:** Concrete evidence that B\u2019s decision\u2011making is rapid and accurate, or that his interpersonal style does not cause crew friction, would push me toward B. Conversely, strong evidence that C\u2019s communication difficulties are mitigated by effective crew cooperation (or that his egocentric behavior does not impair safety) could make C the preferred choice. Evidence of effective leadership/teamwork for A or D would also shift the balance. Until such information is available, I cannot commit to a single candidate.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_1\", \"vote\": \"Undecided\"}"}
